The toolkit and the viewer are derived uses of those rectangles: colours and
measures are added, no coordinate is inferred or altered, and no manuscript
scan image is stored. The viewer loads page images from voynichese.com on
request only.

Transliteration (ZL_ivtff_raw.txt and the words of every bundle): the ZL
transliteration of the Voynich manuscript in IVTFF format by René Zandbergen
and Gabriel Landini (ZL3b, 2025-05-13), published at voynich.nu.

Natural-language comparison texts (data/controls/texts): OCR transcriptions of
early printed herbals and medical texts and training splits of a reference
corpus, assembled for the research workspace; they are provided for the
layout controls only.

Page scans (measured by vmsspatial.images and vmsspatial.ink, never stored
in this repository): Beinecke Rare Book and Manuscript Library, Yale
University, Beinecke MS 408 (the Voynich manuscript), digital images served
by Yale University Library's digital collections under the IIIF Image API
(https://collections.library.yale.edu/catalog/2002046). The toolkit downloads
them into a cache outside the repository on request and keeps only numbers
measured on them.
